  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.3. Proportion of draft laws and/or policies on VAWG, which have received significant inputs from women&#x2019;s rights advocates.
1.1.6. Number of assessments completed on pending topics and strategic litigation implemented by women&#xb4;s rights advocates
1.1.5 Number of Parliamentarians and staff of human rights institutions with strengthened capacities to advocate for, draft new and/or strengthen existing legislation and/or policies on VAWG , including the promotion of women and girls SRHR, and implement the same</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique has the 10th highest rate of early marriage, with 48% of women between 20-24 having gotten married before 18 years of age
37.2% of women aged 15-49 years have suffered some sort of violence (physical or sexual)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Legal revision of relevant GBV legislation
- Training of stakeholders of GBV legislation</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 6 Laws Approved, 2 Resolutions approved and 3 Regulations waiting for final endorsement namely Law n. 19/2019 on Prevention and Combat of Child Marriage, Law n.26/2019 on Alternative Measures of Prison, Law n. 23/ 2019 on Succession Bill, Law n. 22/ 2019 on the Family Law, Law n. 24/ 2019 on the Revision of Penal Code, Law n.25/ 2019 on the Revision of the Penal Code Process. Resolutions approved: Resolution n.39/2020 &#x201c;Gender Strategy in the Public Administration II 2020-2024&#x201d; and Resolution n.28/2020 of 29th April &#x201c;HIV and AIDS Strategy in the Public Administration II 2020-2024&#x201d; . Regulations Developed and Awaiting the final process of validation the following Legislation: Religious Freedom Law, Code of Conduct and the Regulation of the Law of Religious Freedom. 
- A total of 1,086 Justice Officials were trained on the new and revised laws approved aiming to build their skills on law reinforcement and implementation: namely, Supreme Court Judges 585; Attorney General Office 177; National Human Rights Commission 29, Ombudsman 6, SERNIC, 37, CFJJ 30. Ministry of Interior ( PRM- Women Network- 182 and ACIPOL, ESAPOL and EFPMatalana- 40).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Training of Justice System Administration Institutions (SERNIC, Parliament and Police) in 6 GBV, SRH Relevant Laws approved
- Database for PGR and SERNIC: Acquisition of Equipment and training of staff
- Development of 4 Gender Strategies and GBV Plans: MINT, MJCR, SERNIC and Supreme Court</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- A total of 30 trainers police officers (9F and 21M) were trained in the new and revised GBV legislation
- 52 computers were acquired in the scoop of the database for SERNIC and PGR; and a total of 87 staff members from PGR and SERNIC were trained in the new database system
- Ongoing</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
